<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_space",
    "A space always runs in a browser tab of its own, opened with Space beside the conversation's tabs. The map gets the whole window, and the conversation stays exactly where it was."
  )}
</p>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_community}>{dgettext("help_space", "Why a tab of its own")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_space",
    "The map is drawn continuously, and inside the chat it shared the browser with everything the chat was doing. In a tab of its own it does not, which is the difference you feel when several people are walking around at once."
  )}
</p>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_btn_link}>{dgettext("help_space", "The address stays good")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_space",
    "A space has no beginning and no end: it is a place, so bookmarking its address takes you back to it later. Opening it asks the same questions either way — a channel's space wants you in that channel, and a private space belongs to its two people. The tab always shows a way back to the chat along its bottom edge."
  )}
</p>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_community}>{dgettext("help_space", "One tab, not two")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_space",
    "With that address already open somewhere, the entry says In another tab and takes you to the tab you have. A second tab of a world you are standing in would be a second character nobody asked for."
  )}
</p>

<p>
  {dgettext("help_space", "See also:")}
  <.help_link topic="feature-virtual-spaces">
    {dgettext("help_space", "Virtual Spaces")}
  </.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="feature-space-card">
    {dgettext("help_space", "Who Is in the Space Right Now")}
  </.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="feature-space-share">
    {dgettext("help_space", "Inviting Someone to a Space")}
  </.help_link>
</p>
